{
  "id": "alteration-hypothesis",
  "term": "alteration hypothesis",
  "definition": "The alteration hypothesis is the idea that, in focal epilepsy, hippocampal structural abnormalities may develop or worsen over time rather than being fully present at the start of the disorder. In this view, longer disease duration and recurrent seizures are linked to progressive hippocampal change, which may contribute to hippocampal sclerosis.",
